PROJECT: "Vimarsh: Text-to-SQL Clarification Engine" (spec v6.3). Tagline: "Think before you query."

HOW TO USE THIS MESSAGE
This is a multi-stage project and this document is the permanent specification. In THIS message build ONLY Stage 1 (defined at the end). I will request Stages 2-5 in later messages. Never fake behavior: no mock execution, no placeholder SQL results, no invented metrics, no unimplemented security checks.
STAGE REPORT FORMAT: at the end of every stage reply with four short lists: (1) implemented behavior, (2) checks you actually executed and their real results, (3) checks you could not run, (4) known limitations. An unexecuted test counts as unverified. Never claim it passed.

PURPOSE
Users ask data questions in plain English. The AI either (a) generates safe read-only SQL that is validated and executed, (b) asks ONE focused clarifying question when interpretations would give materially different results, or (c) rejects unsafe, off-topic or unanswerable requests. Core principle: NEVER execute a guess.

THREAT MODEL (put this in the README, worded honestly)
- Browser-only educational prototype for one browser and a small synthetic dataset. It is not enterprise-grade.
- Safeguards protect the normal application path. They are NOT proof against a hostile user who controls their own browser (who can inspect client code, modify state, or extract the key they typed).
- Direct browser calls to the Gemini API suit prototyping. Production would need a backend proxy, server-side key management, authorization and resource controls.
- The system prompt is bundled in client code and is NOT secret; it must contain no secrets, and refusing to recite it is best-effort behavior only. Security relies on deterministic code.
- No database rows are ever sent to the LLM.

ARCHITECTURE DECISION (final)
Vimarsh is a browser-only app. Do NOT use the full-stack or server-side runtime: no Node/Express server, no server-side routes, no server secrets. Ignore any platform-provided GEMINI_API_KEY (never read process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY, import.meta.env keys or any secret from the Secrets panel; never add a key to a bundler "define" setting). ALL Gemini calls are made from the browser using ONLY the key the visitor types into the Connect panel. You must NOT make any Gemini API call while generating or testing the code. If you find any server file or key reference, remove it and tell me.

