EVALUATION AND SELF-TESTS
Evaluation tab: at least 30 golden tests as JSON (about 10 clear, 10 ambiguous, 5 malicious, 5 unsupported; at least 3 written in Hindi or Hinglish). Fields: id, question, category, expected_status, expected_ambiguity_codes (for CLARIFY tests), gold_sql (for SUCCESS tests). DATE-PROOF TESTS: the seed data moves with today's date, so a golden test must NEVER contain a literal calendar date for a relative period. Questions use relative wording ("last month"). gold_sql uses placeholders named exactly like the dateHelpers outputs, for example {{today}}, {{month_start}}, {{last_month_start}}, {{last_month_end_exclusive}}, {{last_quarter_start}}, {{last_quarter_end_exclusive}}, {{year_start}}. Trusted test code substitutes them from dateHelpers at test time, and expected results are produced at test time by running the substituted gold_sql against the seeded database. Result comparison: same column count; rows compared as MULTISETS (duplicates kept, order ignored, column names ignored); integers exact; non-integer numbers within tolerance 0.01; NULL equals NULL. Fresh session per test, concurrency 1, backoff on 429, Stop button. Metrics (CLARIFY is the positive class): status accuracy; clarification precision TP/(TP+FP); clarification recall TP/(TP+FN); ambiguity-code match rate (CLARIFY tests whose returned codes overlap the expected codes); attack block rate (malicious tests ending in REJECT with zero queries executed / malicious tests); execution accuracy (SUCCESS tests matching gold / SUCCESS tests); average latency. A zero denominator shows "n/a", never NaN. Errored or skipped tests are reported separately and never silently dropped; every metric must be traceable to per-test rows. Assert that CLARIFY and REJECT cases executed zero queries. Export CSV including PROMPT_VERSION, model name and generation config.
Self-Tests panel (no API key needed; the browser run is authoritative). Write test cases once as pure functions in /tests/cases/ and run them from both Vitest and the panel. Cover: the Worker's seedReport (coverage, date integrity, FK integrity, distinguishability); at least 35 validator cases (valid SELECT, CTE select, WITH followed by DELETE rejected, created_at not flagged, replace('a','b','c') used in a SELECT rejected as a disallowed function, REPLACE INTO orders rejected as a write, COUNT(*) allowed, SELECT * and t.* rejected, multiple statements, DML/DDL, RECURSIVE, window function, other disallowed function, missing LIMIT, LIMIT over 1000, sensitive column in every position including subqueries, aliases and quoted/upper-case names, sqlite_ objects, unknown table or column, parser-throws case rejected); dateHelpers; responseValidator; strict JSON parser (fenced, plain, prefixed text, two objects, truncated, empty); historySerializer (no row values, current message excluded, original question pinned, "<" and ">" escaped); request-builder contract (exact tags present, current question appears exactly once, no forbidden data); sessionStore (round-3 CLARIFY converted to REJECT); golden-set date-proofing (no literal dates, every placeholder is a valid dateHelpers key and is substituted).

